    <statement><p>Find the partial derivative indicated.
Assume the variables are restricted to a domain on
which the function is defined.
<me>z = \sin\mathopen{}\left(4x^{3}y-3xy^{3}\right).</me>
 
<m>z_x =</m> <fillin characters="65" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(12x^{2}y-3y^{3}\right)\cos\mathopen{}\left(4x^{3}y-3xy^{3}\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>z_x = \left(12x^{2}y-3y^{3}\right)\cos\mathopen{}\left(4x^{3}y-3xy^{3}\right).</me>



